te":"aye"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Intellectual Property Laws Amendment (Productivity Commission Response Part 2 and Other Measures) Bill 2019 - in Committee - Maintain innovative patents","noes":12,"question":"The majority voted in favour of leaving [schedule 1](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;db=LEGISLATION;id=legislation%2Fbills%2Fs1216_first-senate%2F0001;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbills%2Fs1216_first-senate%2F0000%22;rec=0) of the bill unchanged. In parliamentary jargon, they voted \"*that schedule 1 stand as printed.*\" This vote occurred after South Australian Senator [Rex Patrick](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/rex_patrick) (Centre Alliance) [proposed that that schedule](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2019-10-16.53.1) should be opposed. ### What does schedule 1 do? According to the [bills digest](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd1920a/20bd042), Schedule 1 phases out the innovation patent system: > *The innovation patent was introduced in 2001 to provide a lower cost, lower inventive threshold, shorter term patent to encourage incremental innovation and to be more accessible to small and medium businesses and private inventors.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-5933","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2019-10-16/2"}
